{"code":"49-9092.00","title":"Commercial Divers","description":"Work below surface of water, using surface-supplied air or scuba equipment to inspect, repair, remove, or install equipment and structures. May use a variety of power and hand tools, such as drills, sledgehammers, torches, and welding equipment. May conduct tests or experiments, rig explosives, or photograph structures or marine life.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.508},"I":{"score":3.6,"share":0.2202},"A":{"score":1.35,"share":0.0296},"S":{"score":1.1,"share":0.0085},"E":{"score":1.66,"share":0.0559},"C":{"score":3.1,"share":0.1778}},"highPoints":["R","I","C"],"tasks":[{"id":13856,"text":"Check and maintain diving equipment, such as helmets, masks, air tanks, harnesses, or gauges.","core":true,"importance":4.72,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.5},{"id":13855,"text":"Take appropriate safety precautions, such as monitoring dive lengths and depths and registering with authorities before diving expeditions begin.","core":true,"importance":4.63,"relevance":96.18,"frequency":5.45},{"id":13854,"text":"Communicate with workers on the surface while underwater, using signal lines or telephones.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.36},{"id":13857,"text":"Descend into water with the aid of diver helpers, using scuba gear or diving suits.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":79.55,"frequency":4.67},{"id":13859,"text":"Inspect and test docks, ships, buoyage systems, plant intakes or outflows, or underwater pipelines, cables, or sewers, using closed circuit television, still photography, and testing equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":95.67,"frequency":3.58},{"id":13858,"text":"Obtain information about diving tasks and environmental conditions.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":94.99,"frequency":4.9},{"id":20809,"text":"Inspect the condition of underwater steel or wood structures.","core":true,"importance":4.09,"relevance":95.56,"frequency":3.52},{"id":13866,"text":"Operate underwater video, sonar, recording, or related equipment to investigate underwater structures or marine life.","core":true,"importance":3.97,"relevance":90.46,"frequency":3.94},{"id":13860,"text":"Repair ships, bridge foundations, or other structures below the water line, using caulk, bolts, and hand tools.","core":true,"importance":3.92,"relevance":97.36,"frequency":3.27},{"id":13861,"text":"Cut and weld steel, using underwater welding equipment, jigs, and supports.","core":true,"importance":3.91,"relevance":95.05,"frequency":3.21},{"id":13872,"text":"Carry out non-destructive testing, such as tests for cracks on the legs of oil rigs at sea.","core":true,"importance":3.88,"relevance":75.67,"frequency":2.84},{"id":13864,"text":"Take test samples or photographs to assess the condition of vessels or structures.","core":true,"importance":3.83,"relevance":94.97,"frequency":3.52},{"id":13871,"text":"Supervise or train other divers, including hobby divers.","core":true,"importance":3.8,"relevance":72.3,"frequency":3.87},{"id":13870,"text":"Perform activities related to underwater search and rescue, salvage, recovery, or cleanup operations.","core":true,"importance":3.78,"relevance":93.55,"frequency":3.24},{"id":13862,"text":"Recover objects by placing rigging around sunken objects, hooking rigging to crane lines, and operating winches, derricks, or cranes to raise objects.","core":true,"importance":3.73,"relevance":91.68,"frequency":3.35},{"id":13865,"text":"Install, inspect, clean, or repair piping or valves.","core":true,"importance":3.72,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.42},{"id":13869,"text":"Set or guide placement of pilings or sandbags to provide support for structures, such as docks, bridges, cofferdams, or platforms.","core":true,"importance":3.72,"relevance":87.6,"frequency":2.9},{"id":13873,"text":"Drill holes in rock and rig explosives for underwater demolitions.","core":false,"importance":3.72,"relevance":32.53,"frequency":null},{"id":